      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nIf you are a current University of Tampa student, please search for and apply to student jobs here via Workday. Job applications for current students will not be considered if submitted through the external career center. Position Details The Department of Physics and Astronomy in the College of Natural and Health Sciences at The University of Tampa invites applications for the position of part-time instructor for the General Physics Laboratory courses. The Department of Physics and Astronomy is a vibrant and growing group of faculty, instructors, and students, and we are looking for qualified candidates to join our team. Responsibilities will include: 1. Teach one or more 2-hour General Physics Laboratories per week for a semester. Experiments follow the syllabus and laboratory manual prepared by the physics faculty. 2. Explain to the students the experiments and expectations for each lab. 3. Assist students with apparatus set-up and data collection. 4. Set up and take down laboratory equipment as appropriate. 5. Provide meeting time for students. 6. Grade and return lab reports/worksheets to students in a timely fashion. 7. Submit final grades to physics lecture instructor(s). The successful candidate will have: 1.  A minimum of a Master's Degree in physics or related field. 2.  Experience teaching introductory physics labs with PASCO or equivalent electronic probes and computer interfaces preferred. Required Attachments Please be sure to attach all required documents listed below in the attachment box at the bottom of the \"My Experience\" page of the application before continuing through the application. Cover Letter Curriculum vitae Additional Information Applications for part-time positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the department when openings become available.  Future teaching assignments are on a term-by-term basis which may include fall, spring 